## Hypothesis D1: Round-count vs security tradeoff (3r/5r/6r SPN)
- **Precise description:** 4r keyed SPN (rasC2_0/pba19/lin(5,13)) is the baseline at 26.5u. Test 3r, 5r, 6r variants with identical per-round construction.
- **Expected mechanism:** Per-round cost ~6.6u (26.5/4). 3r → ~19.8u (matches al_chi6b S0!); 5r → ~33u; 6r → ~40u. Security: fewer rounds = shorter differential trails = higher S2 kill risk. The question is whether 3r with lin(5,13) still passes S2, or if a stronger linear layer is needed.
- **Test:** Generate .v for 3r/5r/6r variants. S0 for delay. If 3r S0 < 22u, run S1+S2 to check if security holds.
- **Status:** SPECS DESIGNED (see gen_batch5.py). Holding S0 launch for load < 4.

