## Hypothesis D3: Key-schedule × linear-layer stacking (batch-6 design)
- **Precise description:** Batch-4 proved ks affects critical path (norc/smallrc/rot1: -0.2u on lin(5,13)). Batch-1 proved lin(5,9) ties lin(5,13) at 26.3u. Test if ks gains STACK with different linear layers: norc/smallrc/rot1 × lin(5,9), lin(8,15).
- **Expected mechanism:** If ks and linear layer affect different parts of the critical path, gains should be additive. If they collide on the same path, no stacking.
- **Non-duplication:** Hybrid owns P-box × linear co-design. This is ks × linear, a different axis.
- **Test:** 3 ks leads × 2 lin leads = 6 combos. S0 first; if any < 26.1u, run S1+S2.
