## 2026-10-10 ~05:30 CEST — D8 COMPLETE (analytic pivot, design worker)

### 1. Invariant-subspace characterization (the "linear invariant" is a diffusion defect)
- Built exact per-round instrumentation (bit-exact vs model.py on 3 controls) + fast S1-LIN D screen (real lin_diff.lin_cell_logp, ~6s/candidate).
- **nolin (dd9_scsc_nolin_a)**: on 64-consecutive inputs, outputs have LOW ALGEBRAIC DEGREE in the 6 varying input bits — 18 constant output bits, degree hist {0:18,1:3,2:4,3:16,4:19,5:4}, block rank ~25 (nullity ~40). Root cause: after S-box round 0 only 8 bit positions vary (P-images of nibbles 0-1); support grows too slowly (8→22→28→51) for the nonlinear layers to build degree. Random-64-input rank is full (63-64) — the defect is specific to consecutive (low-entropy) inputs, which is exactly what S1-LIN tests.
- **single-rot[13] (dd10_scsc_singlerot_a)**: D=1923/4096, rank ~61 (mild but lethal). Degree profile looks healthy (4-6), so this is a DIFFERENT mechanism. x^rotl(x,13) is 2-to-1 (kernel {0,ONES}) forcing even parity, but the bijective passthrough variant (rot13p63) still gives D=1659 — so it is NOT just bijectivity; the 1-XOR rotation structure itself is inadequate.
- **lin(5,13)**: D=20/4096 (null), rank 63-64, degrees 4-6, no constants. Clean.

### 2. Cheapest provably-working linear layer (exhaustive analytic screen, key=0)
- ALL bijective 2-XOR rotation pairs PASS on all rounds: [5,13] D=20, [13,27] D=19, [1,2] D=20, [7,19] D=16. Multi-key (0/FFF/1234) clean for [5,13] (20,19,24).
- ALL 1-XOR variants FAIL: rot13 D=1923, shift1 D=3631, shift31 D=4096, rot13p63 D=1659, rot13p0 D=1449. shift7 D=31 borderline (not robust).
- Partial placements FAIL: lin513/sbox-only D=281, chi-only dead (D7), drop-r1 D=281, drop-r2 D=28(borderline). Drop-last-round is rank-invariant (D identical) BUT the last LIN is load-bearing for the DIFF test (low-8-bit marginal): CSC drop-last DIFF probe worst|z|=938 vs 28 with LIN.
- **Verdict**: the cheapest S1-viable LIN is a 2-XOR rotation pair on ALL rounds (~1.9u/round). 1-XOR cannot do it (proven: x^P(x) never bijective; bijective 1-XOR still fails empirically).

### 3. Breakthrough + scoped negative: 3-round chi-first
- 3-round CHI-FIRST patterns with full 2-XOR LIN are LIN-clean: CSC D=27, CCS D=25, CSS D=27 (multi-key). Sbox-first 3-round (SCS/SSC) is LIN-dead (D=4096). Mechanism: chi-first spreads the 6 varying bits before the nibble-structured S-box round.
- BUT all 3-round are DIFF-dead at real S1 sensitivity: local S1 (real code, 10 keys) → LIN 0/10 rej, DIFF 8-10/10 rej. Specific deltas (2^0,2^3,2^7,2^14) collapse. 3 rounds insufficient for differential diffusion.
- Triple co-design: CHI_A near-optimal; CHI_B (wide) catastrophic (D=3720); wideA slightly better DIFF probe but cannot save 3-round.

### 4. Batch-11 (4 candidates, all <28u, NOT submitted to GHA)
